From 389e9fd7c58c6bc6f02512dddd985a4e5c5b9ee9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cyril Rohr <hey@cyrilrohr.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 09:06:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] solver: reuse imported cache remotes when exporting

When a remote cache export reaches a record that came from an imported
cache, ExportTo loads the result into the local cache (FromRemote, then
GetByBlob with several bolt commits per record) and resolves its remotes
again. runCacheExporters always sets a compression option, so this
happens for every imported record, although resolving a remote without
forced compression keeps the blobs it already has. On warm mode=max
exports, "preparing build cache for export" grows with the number of
imported records while no blob changes.

Reuse the imported remote unless the export forces a compression that
the remote does not have. Forced gzip and eStargz exports still load the
result: the two share a media type, so only the blob content tells them
apart.

Loading the result also turned the registry importer's
containerd.io/distribution.source.ref annotation into the
containerd.io/distribution.source.<host> annotation that the pusher
uses for cross-repository mounts. Do that conversion when marshaling
the cache instead, with a helper now shared with getRemote, so the
exported manifests do not change.

Signed-off-by: Cyril Rohr <hey@cyrilrohr.com>
